## What

Adds an opt-in activity summary to the single-item read endpoint so the item detail view can show recent comment engagement inline.

Requesting `GET /items/:collection/:pk?summary=activity` now attaches a `comment_activity` object to the item payload:

```json
{
  "data": {
    "...item fields...",
    "comment_activity": {
      "comment_count": 4,
      "latest_comment": {
        "comment": "Looks good to me",
        "date_created": "2026-08-14T10:12:00Z",
        "user_created": "a1b2..."
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Why

The item detail view currently has to make a second round-trip to `/comments` just to show how many comments an item has and what the most recent one is. Folding a small summary into the detail read removes that extra request for the common "show engagement at a glance" case.

## Notes

- The summary is only computed when `?summary=activity` is passed, so the default read path is unchanged.
- `latest_comment` is `null` when the item has no comments.
- Scoped to the item detail route (`GET /items/:collection/:pk`); listing endpoints are untouched.

